### Page 1 of 1

```text
Zoning Map Amendment Criteria for
Plains Industrial Park

The applicant is requesting a rezoning of the lot from its current A-2 zone to the AG and HI
zone.  This project is on primarily undeveloped land that has an existing platted dirt road called
HR Ranch Road.  This road will be paved with development.  The AG zone is being requested as
a holding zone until such time that there is a development request for the site.  The HI zone is
requested for an above ground tank farm for Plains All American Pipeline Company.  The
Comprehensive plan calls for Industrial development in the area which HI is usable zone.  The
area to the south is zoned HI as well as GDC Development and most of the Cheyenne Leads
Industrial Park.  It is assumed that the AG lots will also be zoned HI or another commercial zone
at the time of development.   The primary reason for the zone change is to allow industrial
development on the lots which is not allowed in the A-2 zone.  The AG zone change is because
there is no A-2 zone in the UDC.  The development will be able to be developed according to the
subdivision standards for HI as well as meet the intent and applicability of the HI district.  Future
development of the property will be required to go through additional City applications as well
as some State procedures.  This application will not harm the public health, safety or general
welfare of the public.
```
